From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashwin Devi Srinivasan <ashwin@ashds.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:32:10 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the custom watermark without MiSys

On surya the app first writes the device watermark to persist through
MiSys and only keeps its own copy when that write succeeds. Nothing on
this device reads the persist copy: the app draws the device watermark
itself from its files directory. Without MiSys the local copy was never
written and capturing with the watermark crashed the snapshot renderer.
Skip the persist write and always keep the local copy.
---
 smali_classes2/com/android/camera/watermark/gen2/WaterMarkUtil2.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/watermark/gen2/WaterMarkUtil2.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/watermark/gen2/WaterMarkUtil2.smali
index f4ac721..1c1dbfe 100644
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/watermark/gen2/WaterMarkUtil2.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/watermark/gen2/WaterMarkUtil2.smali
@@ -2085,7 +2085,7 @@
 
     const/16 v5, 0x5a
 
-    if-eqz v4, :cond_0
+    goto :cond_0
 
     .line 5
     new-instance v0, Ljava/io/ByteArrayOutputStream;
